course: dictionary
lesson: 1334
title: Context clues: the camel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The dictionary gives two meanings for camel: a large desert animal, and a light brown colour. «Traders travelled in caravans of camels, which can go a long time without drinking, across the Gobi and Taklamakan deserts.» The words travelled, caravans and deserts tell you that camel means the animal here.
explain: Now read this one: «The camel coat was warm and soft.» There is no animal in the sentence, just a coat, so camel must mean the light brown colour. Ask yourself which meaning fits the words around it.
explain: Context also helps you understand the other words in a sentence. «A camel's hump stores fat, not water, which gives energy when food is short.» The clue is that the fat gives energy when food is short, so stores must mean keeps for later. Check it by swapping in "keeps for later" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A camel is a large animal with a long neck and one or two humps on its back.
fact: Camels live in deserts, and they can go many days without drinking.
fact: A camel's hump stores fat, not water, so it gives energy when food is short.
fact: Camel is also a light brown colour.
fact: A thirsty camel can drink up to 100 litres at once.
exercise: «Traders travelled in caravans of camels, which can go a long time without drinking.» What does camels mean here? | A type of cloth | A kind of boat | *Large desert animals with long necks | A light brown colour
exercise: «The camel coat was warm and soft.» Which meaning of camel fits this sentence? | A kind of sand | *A light brown colour | A large animal with humps | A desert town
exercise: «A camel's hump stores fat, not water.» What does the hump store? | *Fat | Water | Food for the rider | Sand
test: Why can camels go many days without drinking? | Because they drink sea water | *Because their bodies waste very little water | Because they carry their own food | Because they sleep all day
test: «The camel's hump sags as the fat is used up.» What does sags mean? | Gets bigger and rounder | Shines in the sun | *Droops or hangs down | Turns light brown
exam: Maya says camel always means an animal, so how should you read «The camel coat was warm and soft»? | Maya is right, because it is an animal | It means a kind of sand | *Maya is wrong, because camel here means a light brown colour | Camel means a warm, soft desert town
